---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
const sections = [["operator", "Who operates Doer"], ["local", "Tasks and local files"], ["google", "Google and Gmail"], ["providers", "AI providers and sharing"], ["retention", "Retention and deletion"], ["website", "Website and support"], ["choices", "Your choices"], ["updates", "Changes and contact"]] as const;
---
<LegalPage title="Privacy Policy - Doer" description="How Doer handles tasks, local files, Gmail connections, and your privacy choices." heading="Doer Privacy Policy" lede="Doer runs tasks on your computer using the AI providers and tools you choose. This policy explains where your information goes and how to disconnect connected tools." effectiveDate="2026-10-04" lastUpdated="2026-10-05" sections={sections}>
  <section id="operator">
    <h2>Who operates Doer</h2>
    <p>Doer and <a href="https://doer.lagaryan.click">doer.lagaryan.click</a> are operated by Aryan Gupta. Contact <a href="mailto:aryangupta4feb@gmail.com">aryangupta4feb@gmail.com</a> for privacy and support requests. Doer is an independent open-source product built on MIT-licensed T3 Code. T3 Tools, Inc. is the upstream copyright holder, not the operator of Doer.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="local">
    <h2>Tasks and local files</h2>
    <p>Task messages, attachments, settings, history, and connected-tool results are stored on the computer running your Doer server. A remote device connects to that computer; it does not move the task into a Doer-operated cloud account. People and devices you pair with your server may access its tasks and enabled tools, so pair only devices you trust.</p>
    <p>Spreadsheet and presentation tools read and edit files in a Space you select. They do not require a Microsoft account or connect to Microsoft 365. Before replacing a document, Doer saves an original copy in that Space's .doer-backups folder. File contents used in a task may be transmitted to the AI provider you select.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="google">
    <h2>Google and Gmail</h2>
    <p>Gmail is optional. When you connect it, Google handles sign-in in your browser. Doer receives your Google email address to identify the connected account and OAuth access and refresh tokens to send messages you approve. Doer does not receive your Google password.</p>
    <p>Doer requests <code>openid</code>, <code>email</code>, and <code>gmail.send</code>. The Gmail permission allows sending mail; it does not allow Doer to read your inbox. Before each send, Doer displays the sending account, recipients, subject, and body and requires your approval for that specific email. Gmail receives the approved message and its recipients to deliver it.</p>
    <p>Gmail tokens are encrypted on the host computer. The desktop encryption key is protected by the operating system's credential storage. Other host setups must supply a securely managed encryption key; sign-in is disabled when secure storage is unavailable. Tokens are used only to maintain the connection and send approved email, and are not supplied to model providers by the connector.</p>
    <p>Doer's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including its Limited Use requirements. Google user data is not sold, used for advertising, or used by Doer to train general-purpose AI models. The operator does not routinely access your connected Google account or its local tokens.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="providers">
    <h2>AI providers and sharing</h2>
    <p>Your selected provider may receive your prompts, file contents, tool results, and conversation context as needed for the task. Its own privacy, retention, and model-training terms apply. Review those terms before using sensitive information. Connecting Gmail does not itself give a model direct access to the Gmail tokens or inbox.</p>
    <p>Doer does not automatically upload your local task database or Gmail credentials to its operator. If you submit a support request, you choose what to share. Please remove passwords, tokens, and sensitive task content from logs and examples. Information you provide for support is used to respond, investigate the reported issue, and meet applicable legal obligations.</p>
    <p>Software downloads and updates use GitHub and npm. Connections to Google, your chosen providers, and services you enable are governed by those services' policies. Operators of servers you choose to connect to are responsible for their own hosting and data practices.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="retention">
    <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>Gmail credentials remain on the host until you disconnect or remove them. Disconnect attempts to revoke Google access before deleting the local credentials. If revocation fails, Doer reports the failure and keeps the credentials so you can retry. You can also revoke access directly in <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">your Google account's third-party connections</a>.</p>
    <p>Disconnecting Gmail does not delete task history, email review records, document backups, or mail already delivered to Gmail or recipients. Local history and backups remain until you delete them; operating-system backups may retain copies. Provider and recipient copies follow their own retention rules. Uninstalling the app may leave local application data.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="website">
    <h2>Website and support</h2>
    <p>Our website hosting and delivery services process technical information such as IP addresses and HTTP request details to serve the site and maintain security. Contacting us by email shares your address and the contents you send. Doer does not require a separate Doer cloud account to use local tasks.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="choices">
    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>You can leave any integration switched off, choose a different AI provider, disconnect Gmail, remove paired devices, and delete local task data and document backups. Switching Gmail off stops the connector from sending in that Space but keeps the Google connection until you disconnect it. For access, correction, or deletion of information you have sent to the operator, contact the email above. Rights and exceptions depend on applicable law.</p>
    <p>Doer is intended for general work and personal tasks, not for children under 13. Do not submit children's personal information to the operator.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="updates">
    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>We will update this policy when data practices change and change the date above. New uses of Google data require updated disclosure and consent before use. Questions can be sent to <a href="mailto:aryangupta4feb@gmail.com">aryangupta4feb@gmail.com</a>.</p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
